{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 16, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Whirlwind Week in Japan**\n\nLast month, I finally took the leap and visited Japan for the first time. A week wasn’t nearly enough, but it gave me a delicious taste of its wonders.\n\nTokyo dazzled with its neon lights and endless energy. I lost myself in Shibuya’s scramble crossing, marveled at the serene Meiji Shrine, and sipped matcha in a tiny café in Kagurazaka. The food? Life-changing. Fresh sushi at Tsukiji Outer Market, crispy tonkatsu, and a conveyor-belt curry that hit the spot after a long day.\n\nA quick shinkansen (bullet train) ride later, I found myself in Kyoto. Temples and traditional tea houses painted a quieter picture. Fushimi Inari’s torii gates left me breathless, and the bamboo forest in Arashiyama felt like stepping into another world. A geisha spotting in Gion was the icing on the cake.\n\nOsaka was all about the laughs and the eats. Dotonbori’s street food stalls tempted me with takoyaki and okonomiyaki, while Universal Studios Japan provided a playful escape. The locals’ kindness—whether helping me with train tickets or bowing politely—made the trip even warmer.\n\nJapan is a paradox: hyper-modern yet deeply rooted in tradition, frenetic yet peaceful. I left with a suitcase full of souvenirs and a heart full of memories—and a desperate need to return.\n\nNext time? A month. No excuses.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.10421782732009888}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.06586650013923645}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.3343368470668793}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -1.7404405298293568e-05}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Week", "logprob": -2.442596912384033}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -3.6954811548639555e-06}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.003386360127478838}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logprob": -0.0017596489051356912}, {"token": "Last", "logprob": -0.44673651456832886}, {"token": " mon